Yes, you can write the contents of a DataOutputStream to a byte array or a String using ByteArrayOutputStream and ByteArrayInputStream. Here's an example:

<pre><code>ByteArrayOutputStream baos = new ByteArrayOutputStream();
// write data to the DataOutputStream 'output'
output.writeByte(1);
output.writeInt(12345);
output.writeUTF("hello world");
// get the contents of the DataOutputStream as a byte array
byte[] byteArray = baos.toByteArray();
// convert the byte array to a String
String string = new String(byteArray, StandardCharsets.UTF_8);
// or create an input stream from the byte array
ByteArrayInputStream bais = new ByteArrayInputStream(byteArray);
</code></pre>

Note: It's important to use the same charset when converting the byte array to a String, as the default charset may not be the same as the one used by writeUTF(). In this example, we used StandardCharsets.UTF_8.

