    // address1, address2, city, state, etc.

    @OneToMany(mappedBy = "billingAddress")
    private Set<Order> billedOrders;

    @OneToMany(mappedBy = "shippingAddress")
    private Set<Order> shippedOrders;

    // getters and setters
}
```

In this example, we're using the `mappedBy` attribute to specify the inverse side of the bidirectional relationship - in this case, the `Order` entity. The `billedOrders` and `shippedOrders` fields represent the orders that use the address as the billing and shipping address, respectively. 

Note that we're using separate `@OneToMany` annotations for the two sides of the bidirectional relationship - one for billing, and one for shipping. This is necessary because the two sides use different column names (`billing_address_id` and `shipping_address_id`). 

