Here's a sample code that creates directories starting from 'a' to 'z' and max depth of 3 levels:

```
import java.io.File;

public class CreateDirectories {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        String rootDir = "C:\\mydirectory\\"; // replace with your desired root directory path
        int maxDepth = 3;
        int count = 0;
        createDirectories(rootDir, maxDepth, count);
    }

    private static void createDirectories(String dir, int maxDepth, int count) {
        if (count < maxDepth) {
            for (char c = 'a'; c <= 'z'; c++) {
                String newDir = dir + c + "\\";
                File file = new File(newDir);
                if (!file.exists()) {
                    if (file.mkdir()) {
                        System.out.println("Directory created: " + newDir);
                        createDirectories(newDir, maxDepth, count + 1);
                    } else {
                        System.out.println("Failed to create directory: " + newDir);
                    }
                }
            }
        }
    }
}
```

This code will create directories from 'a' to 'z' at the root directory, then for each directory created, it will create subdirectories from 'a' to 'z' until it reaches the max depth specified. If a directory already exists, it will not be created and will skip to the next character. 

Note: Make sure to replace the root directory path with your desired path.

