     }  
     vector_of_functions = c(vector_of_functions, f(i))  
}
</code></pre>

In this example, the function <code>f</code> is a closure that returns a new function with the appropriate coefficient value. We pass the coefficient value to <code>f</code>, creating a new function for each iteration of the loop.

Note that the new function returned by <code>f</code> is defined using a shorthand notation for anonymous functions in R. It's equivalent to:

<pre><code>function(number) {  
     return(coefficient*number)  
